# Cursor Rules for AetherDeck

1. Code Quality & Modularity:
- Always use TypeScript with explicit types; avoid `any`.
- Keep components modular and atomic under `/components`.
- Separate visual renderers by tier (`/renderers/tier-basic`, `/renderers/tier-plus`, `/renderers/tier-pro`).

2. Performance & 3D:
- Ensure Three.js / WebGL canvases are lazy-loaded (`next/dynamic` with `ssr: false`) to avoid hydration errors.
- Dispose of WebGL materials and geometries properly upon unmounting.

3. Fallbacks:
- Always provide fallback mock data if `process.env.OPENAI_API_KEY` is not present, allowing local preview without crashing.